## If Phase A reveals MISO_ILLINOIS is fundamentally wrong

If the investigation in Phase A shows MISO_ILLINOIS is a
copy-paste error from PJM_COMED and the "correct" value is
essentially 0, decide:

(a) Keep MISO_ILLINOIS in the analysis with ~0 MW capacity,
    which makes it functionally equivalent to MISO_MS and
    MISO_TEXAS (placeholder zones). It still has a legitimate
    stress signal from whatever Ameren IL hub it's sourced from.
(b) Remove MISO_ILLINOIS from the analysis entirely. Drops the
    destination count from 19 to 18. Methods ¶45 needs updating.

Recommendation: (a). Keeps the paper's "19 destinations" claim
intact (even though 3 are now zero-capacity placeholders), and
the stress signal is real data worth preserving for the
correlation analysis even if its capacity contribution is zero.

## Draft Methods ¶45 replacement (for the polish pass)

> "Destination headroom is calculated from a dataset mapping data
> center operational capacity (as of [VINTAGE DATE]) to pricing
> zones across four grid regions: PJM (8 zones), ERCOT (4 zones),
> CAISO (2 zones), MISO (6 zones with dedicated hub LMP publication),
> and NYISO (5 zones). Two MISO load-resource zones with significant
> operational capacity — MISO Zone 2 (Wisconsin, ~24 MW operational,
> ~7.6 GW announced buildout) and MISO Zone 5 (Missouri, ~411 MW
> operational, ~3.4 GW total) — are excluded from the destination
> pool because MISO does not publish dedicated day-ahead LMPs for
> these zones. Sensitivity analysis including these zones via
> neighboring-hub LMP proxies is reported in Extended Data Table X.
> Of the 19 included destination zones, three (MISO_ILLINOIS,
> MISO_MS, MISO_TEXAS) carry zero mapped DC capacity at the time
> of this analysis and function as price-signal placeholders. The
> remaining 16 zones with nonzero capacity total X MW of aggregate
> destination headroom. Individual zones' LMP coverage windows
> range from January 2022 through December 2025 (earliest-starting
> zones) to November 2022 through September 2025 (CAISO zones);
> hours outside a destination zone's coverage window are treated
> as available in the conditional Monte Carlo (its rated capacity
> contributes to headroom). Extended Data Table Y reports
> sensitivity to the alternative strict-exclusion convention."

## Draft Methods §X new paragraph on DC capacity data vintage

> "Data center capacity values are sourced from [DATASET NAME],
> a point-in-time snapshot of announced, under-construction, and
> operational data center facilities mapped to counties across
> North America, covering [N] facilities totaling [X] GW across
> all phases as of [VINTAGE DATE]. For the primary analysis, we
> use operational capacity only — facilities that are energized
> and contributing load to the grid at snapshot time. This
> reflects the destination pool actually available to an operator
